fix(ui): F-0019 Sensor status is written out, not colour only

Finding:     F-0019 (P0, WCAG 1.4.1 / A11Y-19). Same cells, same cause: F-0025 (P0),
             F-0032 (P0), F-0020 (P1, WCAG 1.1.1 - cells empty to screen readers).
             Each Status cell was a bare coloured dot: colour-blind growers could not
             tell which sensor needs attention and screen readers heard nothing.
Originating: Status cells state their status in text, distinguishable in the
             deuteranopia/protanopia/achromatopsia captures; the ARIA snapshot gives
             each cell a name.
Regression:  journey switch-dosing-to-manual; audit axe,layout,contrast,census,keyboard
             at 320-1440; ARIA diff (names gained only).
Drift class: local defect -> visible word after each dot; dot marked aria-hidden.
Layer:       index.html (5 Status cells), styles.css (.dot margin-right: 8px).
Assumptions: the words "OK", "Warning", "Alarm" restate the three states the page
             already encodes (dot--ok / dot--warn / dot--alarm). They add no new
             fact; reword if the farm uses other terms on the bay-door checklist.
Left alone:  what the float alarm means and what to do (F-0063, blocked on the growing
             lead). Cosmetic: in the narrow Sensors panel "Warning"/"Alarm" wrap under
             their dot; a nowrap attempt clipped the column and was reverted
             (F-0019-attempt2-REVERTED.diff.txt). Deferred to the debt register.
Re-test:     run 20261007-101620-fix-f-0019: axe/keyboard/layout/contrast 0, journey
             3/3, 0 introduced vs baseline; ARIA cells read OK/Warning/Alarm. PASSED.
Baseline:    665ca185ac74f08453715a82013e960438c2e377; apply after F-0003 and F-0021.

